# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  הכסף שלנו — what does NOT belong in the repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The ministries' spreadsheets are BUILD INPUTS, not source. The workflow
# caches them between runs; 82 files a quarter in git history would bloat the
# repo forever to store something we can re-download in a minute.
reports/*.xlsx
reports/manifest.json

# a stray copy in the project root — it belongs in reports\
/repository-of-answers_*.xlsx

# the raw contract_spending pull. Also a build input: hundreds of MB of the
# same rows the API will hand us again next month.
build/

# LibreOffice / Excel leave these behind while a file is open
.~lock.*#
~$*
*.tmp

# node
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# python leaves these next to any module it imports — the test runs on GitHub
# will make tools/__pycache__ every time
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# leftovers from tidy-up.bat
_old_delete_me/
*.log

# NOTE: site/data/**  IS committed on purpose. Those JSON files are what the
# site actually reads, and what the monthly workflow updates. That is the
# point of putting this on GitHub.
